sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as User (browser)
  participant JS as mercury.js + HTMX
  participant W as Flask web
  participant DB as PostgreSQL
  participant GM as Gmail API

  U->>JS: click a thread row (or press Enter)
  JS->>W: GET /app/threads/<id> (HX-Request: true)
  W->>DB: owned_thread(user_id, id), else 404
  W->>DB: analysis, bucket, message refs (all filtered by user_id)
  W->>DB: set last_opened_at on first open (Gmail unread state untouched)
  W-->>JS: reader partial: subject, AI summary, actions, skeleton for body
  JS->>W: GET /app/threads/<id>/body
  W->>DB: ownership check again
  W->>GM: threads.get format=full (timeout, at most 1 retry)
  alt success
    W->>W: MIME to plain text (skip attachments, HTML converted to text)
    W-->>JS: escaped text, newest first, Cache-Control: no-store
  else deleted
    W-->>JS: 404 "no longer available"
  else access revoked
    W-->>JS: 409 "Reconnect Gmail"
  else Gmail down or rate-limited
    W-->>JS: 503 "temporarily unavailable" + Try again
  end
  Note over W,DB: The message body is never written to the database, queue, logs, or browser storage
